  "reviewNotes": {
    "architecture": "Saved-result acceptance reviewed against f0137167 plus working-tree changes. Only the research/report diagram changes: a completed native result can require local validation/reparse and acceptance of its original turn before advancing. The other four diagrams retain their existing service/owner, simulation, channel publication and real-ledger structure.",
    "behavior": "Completed provider output and accepted research are distinct. Saved-result validation must bind task identity, frozen input and result hash, accept the original turn once and avoid a provider replay or duplicate charge; only a needed subsequent summary is a new model call. Reverse-check evidenceIds allow up to sixty valid supplied IDs, with unknown IDs and sixty-one entries still rejected. No new trading, source or publication authority is introduced; documentation does not certify a live deployment or research result.",
    "tooling": "Complete-portfolio changes do not modify the context helpers or CI integration; their prior verification remains separate from the new application behavior review.",
    "testFixtures": "CI crossed Shanghai midnight: three integration suites now align scenario clocks and dates; stale-report and ledger guards remain unchanged. These test-only changes do not alter any of the five architecture flows.",
    "concurrentMain": "PR #80 (f0fb2a0) inspected during final integration: added saved daily-report recovery, returnedDocumentId and readable simulation review projections. Repository/research references and report diagram updated; other architecture flows unchanged. Date fixture fixes preserve both calendar derivation and deterministic clocks.",
    "completePortfolioResearch": "Reviewed against 65c388e plus working-tree changes on 2026-11-07, not an uncreated release commit. Checked council input packers, resume reservation and correction-bound reverse-check selection, report coverage/body publication, simulation review timestamps and archived/category readers. Retained independent openings are never retroactively labelled complete after supplementation; formatting recovery remains separate from explicit AI continuation.",
    "unchangedFlows": "For saved-result acceptance, diagrams 1, 3, 4 and 5 need no structural changes: route/module/auth/provider boundaries remain the same; strategy confirmation, source/order fences and timestamped simulation observation coverage are unchanged; channel seals/template/deduplication/outbox remain unchanged; no real-ledger/import/reconstruction mutation is introduced.",
    "documentationVerification": "Saved-result acceptance update: context helper tests passed 15 cases with zero skips outside the sandbox restriction on disposable Git metadata. Context checker and whitespace/retrieval checks validate documentation structure only; the working-tree drift warning remains expected. These checks do not certify runtime research or deployment.",
    "savedResultAcceptance": "Reviewed f0137167 plus working-tree changes: assertSavedDailyResult and checkpoint.remote.reparseExisting bind original task identity and SHA-256 promptHash/resultHash/contextHash at reservation and reparseDailyTurn. Normal recordTurn accepts the same turn; old provider calls and budgets are not repeated. A saved challenge needs only a subsequent summary call, while a saved summary can publish with zero new calls. parseDailyReverseCheck now shares the sixty-record inventory bound; unknown/sixty-one references remain invalid. User documentation only corrects the prior unconditional AI-call wording."
  }
